# The API's direct dependencies: the input to the locks (PRD-262 US-022). Nothing
# installs this file. Every image, Railway's included, installs requirements.lock, and
# CI installs requirements.lock with requirements-dev.lock, every pin with its hashes.
# After changing this file or requirements-dev.txt, regenerate the two locks from the
# repository root with the command at the top of each, in this order:
# requirements.lock, requirements-dev.lock.
# The backend suite fails when a lock does not satisfy its input
# (orchestrator/tests/test_prd262_api_locks.py runs scripts/ci/lock_check.py, which
# reads the files and never re-resolves against PyPI).
#
# Core FastAPI dependencies
# The web stack is pinned exactly, as a tested set (F092: an unpinned fresh install
# once served a manifest of about a dozen routes). Since FastAPI 0.137 an included
# router stays ONE entry in app.routes, with no path, instead of a copy of each of
# its routes; anything that walks the routes flattens them with
# fastapi.routing.iter_route_contexts (scripts/dump_routes.py, the rate limiter's
# route lookup, the authz sweep). tests/test_prd262_web_stack.py boots main in a
# fresh process and checks that every router of router_manifest.py answers and that
# no route of reports/route-manifest.json is lost. PRD-262 US-008.
# - starlette 1.0.1 fixes GHSA-86qp-5c8j-p5mr (on CISA's KEV list).
# - uvicorn 0.50.1: its [standard] extra takes websockets>=11.0, so it runs with the
#   13.1 below. Its --workers manager restarts a worker that dies (since 0.30).
fastapi==0.146.0
starlette==1.8.0
uvicorn[standard]==0.50.1
# google-genai needs websockets>=13 (#1169). 13.1 is the last release before 14 deprecated
# the legacy API that uvicorn's default WebSocket protocol (websockets_impl) serves with.
websockets==13.1

