# PRD-126: Business Knowledge Graph (Graphify Integration). Pinned exactly to the
# version `>=0.3.28` resolved to (networkx==3.1 holds it there), so a rebuild can't
# move the graph code under us (PRD-262 US-015). Installed without its [leiden] extra:
# modules/knowledge/leiden_partition.py serves graphify.cluster's Leiden calls from
# graspologic-native, the Rust core graspologic's leiden() forwarded to, so the extra's
# graspologic and the ~585 MB it pulled in (numba, llvmlite, POT, gensim, statsmodels,
# matplotlib, scikit-learn, pandas) are in no image (PRD-262 US-027). The adapter
# replaces graphify's _partition, so a graphifyy bump is checked against it first.
graphifyy==0.8.31
graspologic-native==1.3.1

# PRD-256 (#847): OpenTelemetry traces over OTLP, default OFF (OTEL_ENABLED). Installed
# always, imported only when enabled (core/observability/otel.py). OTLP over HTTP only:
# every collector takes it, and it needs no grpcio. Versions resolved against the
# fastapi/starlette/uvicorn pins above. FastAPI itself requires opentelemetry-api
# (>=1.44) and imports the API at `import fastapi` (fastapi.telemetry), so the off-path
# test takes that as its baseline and checks our code adds nothing. FastAPI's own tracing
# stays off while this instrumentation's middleware is in the stack, so a request still
# makes one server span. 0.66b1 reads FastAPI's route tree through iter_route_contexts,
# so http.route keeps the full template.
opentelemetry-api==1.45.1
opentelemetry-sdk==1.45.1
opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-http==1.45.1
opentelemetry-instrumentation-fastapi==0.66b1
# O2a: the server span's children. botocore's brings opentelemetry-propagator-aws-xray.
opentelemetry-instrumentation-sqlalchemy==0.66b1
opentelemetry-instrumentation-httpx==0.66b1
opentelemetry-instrumentation-redis==0.66b1
opentelemetry-instrumentation-botocore==0.66b1
